 "description": "M4A4 (CS:GO name): Mk 18 Mod 0 CQBR on a Colt M4A1 lower, visual art model. Origin at the bolt face on the bore axis, x to the muzzle, z up, right side -y. Barrel 10.3 in (262 mm) with the KAC M4QD flash hider (front at 312.4 mm, 63 mm ahead of the FSB per the SAR close-up), FSB at the carbine gas position, KAC M4 RAS with 11-rib panels, A.R.M.S. #40 rear sight (raised), LMT SOPMOD stock (190 mm, per the SAR Mk 18 photo) one position out, A2 grip, USGI 30-round magazine. Receiver geometry and every control/pin position follow the leveled PEO Soldier M4 right-side photo (4.52 px/mm from the Picatinny pitch); overall 717.4 mm (SAR Mk 18 Mod 0 photo: about 713 mm) (published Mk 18 Mod 0 with M4 stock 667-679 mm collapsed, 748-762 mm extended; SOPMOD is about 1 in longer than the M4 stock). Widths: buffer tube 1.148 in (29.16 mm), Picatinny 21.2 mm, receivers 29.0 / 24.2 mm and magwell 28.4 mm (estimates), SOPMOD 57.6 mm. The bore is open; the ejection port of the upper receiver and the magazine well are sampled with rays (dust cover and magazine excluded). Engraved markings are booleans in the lower receiver.",
